    "intro_html":  "Bo kho is Vietnamese beef stew, and the two things that make it Vietnamese rather than generic are lemongrass and annatto. The lemongrass gives it that bright citrus edge underneath the beef, and the annatto in the achiote paste turns the broth a deep orange that no amount of tomato could manage. Served over rice noodles, each bowl carries 593 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e33 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$6.83 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
